+  "title": "Planning Food and Guest Flow for a Standing Reception",
+  "body_html": "<p>Food at a standing reception must fit the room and the pace of the gathering. Plan easy-to-hold bites, tray circulation, dietary choices and where guests can put down plates and glasses.</p>\n<p>For the service options, explore <a href=\"/events\">event catering in Dubai</a>. Use this guide to prepare the details for your enquiry.</p>\n<h2>Match the food to how guests move</h2>\n<p>Decide whether bites welcome guests before dinner or make up the main meal. That distinction affects the menu, portions and replenishment. Choose items that can be eaten comfortably while standing, with a clear plan for plates, napkins and used glassware.</p>\n<h2>Map the room before setting service points</h2>\n<p>Keep arrival, drinks and food queues from meeting in the same narrow space. Identify a route for passed trays and somewhere staff can collect used items. Share photographs and a floor plan with the provider rather than estimating circulation from guest count alone.</p>\n<h2>Give dietary dishes a clear route</h2>\n<p>Collect requirements before the menu is agreed. Ask how alternatives will be labelled and offered, and which separation measures are feasible. Do not assume a guest will be able to identify ingredients from appearance or that a shared tray is suitable for every allergy.</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Grazing table set up for a self-served cocktail party\" src=\"https://gwvckixiegkllthleuyt.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/workspace-article-images-public/023d6e8e-8051-428b-8f82-41884070f5e2/body-1b8d5cfe5ca7f3dee27d948717393bba.jpg\" /></p>\n<h2>Build the food schedule around the programme</h2>\n<p>List the arrival period, speeches and any later seated meal. Agree when food service starts, pauses and ends, and whether the menu will be replenished continuously or in waves. The team needs a named contact for changes on the day.</p>\n<h2>Separate food, drinks and equipment</h2>\n<p>Confirm whether the proposal covers food only, food and service staff, or a broader event arrangement. Record bar responsibilities, glassware, ice, serving equipment and cleanup separately. Do not assume alcohol or a staffed bar is included.</p>\n<h2>Choose a service format</h2>\n<p>Use the <a href=\"/cocktail-party-catering-dubai\">cocktail reception service options</a> to compare a passed service with other formats. For a company occasion, the <a href=\"/corporate\">corporate catering team</a> can review the workplace and event brief.</p>",
+  "body_markdown": "Food at a standing reception must fit the room and the pace of the gathering. Plan easy-to-hold bites, tray circulation, dietary choices and where guests can put down plates and glasses.\n\nFor the service options, explore [event catering in Dubai](/events). Use this guide to prepare the details for your enquiry.\n\n## Match the food to how guests move\nDecide whether bites welcome guests before dinner or make up the main meal. That distinction affects the menu, portions and replenishment. Choose items that can be eaten comfortably while standing, with a clear plan for plates, napkins and used glassware.\n\n## Map the room before setting service points\nKeep arrival, drinks and food queues from meeting in the same narrow space. Identify a route for passed trays and somewhere staff can collect used items. Share photographs and a floor plan with the provider rather than estimating circulation from guest count alone.\n\n## Give dietary dishes a clear route\nCollect requirements before the menu is agreed. Ask how alternatives will be labelled and offered, and which separation measures are feasible. Do not assume a guest will be able to identify ingredients from appearance or that a shared tray is suitable for every allergy.\n\n![Grazing table set up for a self-served cocktail party](https://gwvckixiegkllthleuyt.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/workspace-article-images-public/023d6e8e-8051-428b-8f82-41884070f5e2/body-1b8d5cfe5ca7f3dee27d948717393bba.jpg)\n\n## Build the food schedule around the programme\nList the arrival period, speeches and any later seated meal. Agree when food service starts, pauses and ends, and whether the menu will be replenished continuously or in waves. The team needs a named contact for changes on the day.\n\n## Separate food, drinks and equipment\nConfirm whether the proposal covers food only, food and service staff, or a broader event arrangement. Record bar responsibilities, glassware, ice, serving equipment and cleanup separately. Do not assume alcohol or a staffed bar is included.\n\n## Choose a service format\nUse the [cocktail reception service options](/cocktail-party-catering-dubai) to compare a passed service with other formats. For a company occasion, the [corporate catering team](/corporate) can review the workplace and event brief.",
