+  "body_html": "<p>A desert dinner proposal needs a workable location and access plan. Compare venue permission, transport, power, water, preparation space and weather contingencies before choosing a menu.</p>\n<p>For the service options, explore <a href=\"/luxury-dining-experiences\">private dining experiences in Dubai</a>. Use this guide to prepare the details for your enquiry.</p>\n<h2>Confirm the location and permissions</h2>\n<p>Identify the actual venue or managed site, the responsible operator and which permissions apply to your proposed gathering. Do not assume an attractive desert location permits vehicle access, cooking or an event. Agree who is responsible for obtaining and checking the necessary permissions.</p>\n<h2>Check access and transport</h2>\n<p>Share the route, access conditions, arrival point and the time available for unloading. Confirm how guests and the service team reach the site and how equipment leaves afterwards. A dinner proposal should identify transport responsibilities rather than treating the location as an ordinary home delivery.</p>\n<h2>List the facilities</h2>\n<p>Check usable power, lighting, water, handwashing arrangements and preparation space with the venue and provider. Ask how food will be stored and served in those conditions. The menu must fit the facilities actually available, including any restrictions on live cooking.</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Private chef finishing a dish beside a low table set for desert dining at dusk\" src=\"https://gwvckixiegkllthleuyt.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/workspace-article-images-public/d3bc52c2-b6df-40f4-a5bb-9426211a5340/body-b4a38b57c325bd3c20d0275cfa0bf5fc.jpg\" /></p>\n<h2>Agree a weather contingency</h2>\n<p>Discuss the conditions under which the plan needs to change and what alternative is available. Confirm the decision contact and the booking terms for changes. An outdoor photograph is not evidence that a particular setup is appropriate on your date.</p>\n<h2>Compare the full scope</h2>\n<p>Separate the menu, staff, equipment, seating, lighting and venue arrangements. Identify what the provider supplies and what another operator handles. Include the agreed service window, clear-down and waste collection in the same written brief.</p>\n<h2>Move from logistics to the menu</h2>\n<p>Once the site is workable, explore the <a href=\"/desert-dining-dubai\">desert dining service</a>. Share guest numbers, dietary requirements and the desired meal format so the team can assess the complete arrangement.</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Diagram showing five categories of desert dining catering connected to a central desert dining hub\" src=\"https://gwvckixiegkllthleuyt.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/workspace-article-images-public/d3bc52c2-b6df-40f4-a5bb-9426211a5340/body-8189598d7f508bde369e4ce66835da0f.jpg\" /></p>",
+  "body_markdown": "A desert dinner proposal needs a workable location and access plan. Compare venue permission, transport, power, water, preparation space and weather contingencies before choosing a menu.\n\nFor the service options, explore [private dining experiences in Dubai](/luxury-dining-experiences). Use this guide to prepare the details for your enquiry.\n\n## Confirm the location and permissions\nIdentify the actual venue or managed site, the responsible operator and which permissions apply to your proposed gathering. Do not assume an attractive desert location permits vehicle access, cooking or an event. Agree who is responsible for obtaining and checking the necessary permissions.\n\n## Check access and transport\nShare the route, access conditions, arrival point and the time available for unloading. Confirm how guests and the service team reach the site and how equipment leaves afterwards. A dinner proposal should identify transport responsibilities rather than treating the location as an ordinary home delivery.\n\n## List the facilities\nCheck usable power, lighting, water, handwashing arrangements and preparation space with the venue and provider. Ask how food will be stored and served in those conditions. The menu must fit the facilities actually available, including any restrictions on live cooking.\n\n![Private chef finishing a dish beside a low table set for desert dining at dusk](https://gwvckixiegkllthleuyt.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/workspace-article-images-public/d3bc52c2-b6df-40f4-a5bb-9426211a5340/body-b4a38b57c325bd3c20d0275cfa0bf5fc.jpg)\n\n## Agree a weather contingency\nDiscuss the conditions under which the plan needs to change and what alternative is available. Confirm the decision contact and the booking terms for changes. An outdoor photograph is not evidence that a particular setup is appropriate on your date.\n\n## Compare the full scope\nSeparate the menu, staff, equipment, seating, lighting and venue arrangements. Identify what the provider supplies and what another operator handles. Include the agreed service window, clear-down and waste collection in the same written brief.\n\n## Move from logistics to the menu\nOnce the site is workable, explore the [desert dining service](/desert-dining-dubai). Share guest numbers, dietary requirements and the desired meal format so the team can assess the complete arrangement.\n\n![Diagram showing five categories of desert dining catering connected to a central desert dining hub](https://gwvckixiegkllthleuyt.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/workspace-article-images-public/d3bc52c2-b6df-40f4-a5bb-9426211a5340/body-8189598d7f508bde369e4ce66835da0f.jpg)",
