 {
   "slug": "best-gluten-free-catering-companies-in-dubai",
-  "title": "Best gluten-free catering companies in Dubai 2026",
-  "body_html": "<p><strong>Best overall for gluten-free home dining in Dubai: myCHEF</strong>, a private chef service that agrees the menu with you before the chef ever buys an ingredient. <strong>Best for large gluten-free celebrations:</strong> full-service event caterers running a dedicated production kitchen. <strong>Best for office lunches:</strong> drop-off catering specialists with pre-packaged, pre-labelled trays. <strong>Best for turnkey venue packages:</strong> hotel and restaurant catering arms with a standing gluten-free menu already on the books.</p>\n<div class=\"pseo-tldr\" style=\"display:flow-root;clear:both;margin:32px 0;padding:24px 28px;border:1px solid;border-color:rgba(128,128,128,0.35);border-color:color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 14%, transparent);border-left:3px solid;border-left-color:rgba(128,128,128,0.6);border-left-color:color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 30%, transparent);border-radius:12px;background-color:rgba(128,128,128,0.06);background-color:color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 4%, transparent);max-width:100%;\"><div class=\"pseo-tldr-label\" style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:rgba(128,128,128,0.9);color:color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 55%, transparent);margin-bottom:12px;\">TL;DR</div><ul style=\"float:none;margin:0;padding-left:20px;list-style:disc;\"><li style=\"float:none;margin:8px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:inherit;\">myCHEF wins for gluten-free home dining in Dubai because you build the menu with the chef directly, not from a printed card.</li><li style=\"float:none;margin:8px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:inherit;\">Full-service event caterers suit large gluten-free parties that need a dedicated production kitchen.</li><li style=\"float:none;margin:8px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:inherit;\">Drop-off specialists cover office lunches but rely on written allergen labels, not a chef on site.</li><li style=\"float:none;margin:8px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:inherit;\">Hotel and restaurant catering arms offer a tested gluten-free menu with less room to customise.</li></ul></div><h2>Why this matters</h2>\n<p>Gluten intolerance and coeliac disease aren&#39;t a preference to hedge around in Dubai&#39;s catering scene — a mislabelled dish means a genuinely sick guest, not a minor inconvenience. Getting the format wrong for a gluten-free brief in 2026 usually comes down to one thing: how much control you actually have over the kitchen that touches your food.</p>\n<p>A private chef service like <a href=\"https://www.mychef.ae/\">myCHEF&#39;s private chef and catering service</a> puts you in the room while the menu gets built, which matters more for gluten-free guests than for almost any other dietary flag. This guide compares the four real ways to book gluten-free catering in Dubai — private chef, full-service event catering, drop-off trays and hotel catering — so you can match the format to your guest list and risk tolerance, not just to a menu PDF.</p>\n<h2>What makes the best gluten-free catering in Dubai</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ingredient transparency</strong> — you can see or ask about every ingredient before the day, not just read a label at the buffet</li>\n<li><strong>Separate prep, not just separate plating</strong> — cross-contact happens at the chopping board, not the serving tray</li>\n<li><strong>Genuine menu flexibility</strong> — a real gluten-free option on every course, not one token dish</li>\n<li><strong>Halal alignment</strong> — most Dubai households and offices need gluten-free and halal to work together, not as two separate requests</li>\n<li><strong>Staffing that understands the brief</strong> — whoever cooks or plates on the day needs to actually know which dish is gluten-free</li>\n<li><strong>Scale match</strong> — a caterer built for a 200-guest wedding handles a six-person dinner very differently to one built for home dining</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A host planning around these six points ends up choosing a format, not just a menu.</p>\n<h2>Gluten-free catering in Dubai at a glance</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Option</th>\n<th>Best for</th>\n<th>Standout feature</th>\n<th>Key limitation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>myCHEF (private chef)</td>\n<td>Home dining with full menu control</td>\n<td>Menu agreed with the chef before the date</td>\n<td>Not built for 100+ guest events</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Full-service event caterers</td>\n<td>Large gluten-free celebrations</td>\n<td>Dedicated production kitchen at scale</td>\n<td>Menu locked in earlier, less live adjustment</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Drop-off catering specialists</td>\n<td>Office lunches and smaller gatherings</td>\n<td>Pre-packaged trays with allergen labels</td>\n<td>No chef on site for last-minute questions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hotel and restaurant catering arms</td>\n<td>Turnkey venue packages</td>\n<td>Standing gluten-free menu already tested</td>\n<td>Menu fixed to the venue&#39;s existing dishes</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>1. myCHEF: best gluten-free catering for home dining with full menu control</h2>\n<p>myCHEF is a private chef and catering service that sends a vetted chef to cook in your own kitchen, working from a menu you agree together ahead of the booking. For a gluten-free brief, that means the ingredient list gets discussed at the planning stage, not printed on a card next to a buffet. The same chef format covers dinner parties, weekly meal prep, corporate meals and larger home celebrations, so the gluten-free conversation carries across every occasion.</p>\n<p><strong>myCHEF pros:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Menu agreed with the chef before the date, so gluten-free swaps happen at the planning stage</li>\n<li>Cooking happens in your own kitchen, so you can see the ingredients going into each dish</li>\n<li>Halal-first standards run alongside dietary requests instead of as a separate add-on — see the <a href=\"https://www.mychef.ae/blog/best-halal-catering-companies-in-dubai\">halal-first catering standards</a> most Dubai households ask for</li>\n<li>The same format works for a six-person dinner or a larger home celebration</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>myCHEF cons:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Not designed for events running into hundreds of covers</li>\n<li>Kitchen size and equipment in the home can limit some menu choices</li>\n<li>Pricing depends on menu and guest count, so it needs a quote rather than a fixed rate card</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Best for:</strong> households and small offices in Dubai that want a gluten-free menu built around specific guests, not a generic dietary tick-box.</p>\n<p><strong>Verdict: book</strong> if you want the chef to hear your gluten-free requirements directly, before a single ingredient is bought.</p>\n<h2>2. Full-service event caterers: best for large gluten-free celebrations</h2>\n<p>Full-service event caterers in Dubai run a production kitchen away from the venue and plate on site, which becomes useful once a gluten-free guest list runs into the dozens or hundreds. The menu gets fixed further ahead of the date than a private chef booking, because the kitchen is planning a production run rather than a single dinner.</p>\n<p><strong>Full-service caterer pros:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Handles guest counts a home kitchen can&#39;t manage</li>\n<li>Usually offers a tested gluten-free version of most menu items</li>\n<li>Staff on site manage service and plating separately from cooking</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full-service caterer cons:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Menu locked in earlier, with less room for last-minute changes</li>\n<li>Less direct contact with the person actually cooking your food</li>\n<li>Group gluten-free requests get handled as a batch, not a personal brief</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Best for:</strong> weddings, large birthdays and corporate galas in Dubai where gluten-free is one dietary line among several.</p>\n<p><strong>Verdict: consider</strong> this format once your guest count passes what a single private chef can cover.</p>\n<h2>3. Drop-off catering specialists: best for office lunches and smaller gatherings</h2>\n<p>Drop-off caterers prepare trays off site and deliver without staff, which suits a gluten-free office lunch or a casual home gathering where nobody needs course-by-course plating. The gluten-free tray usually arrives labelled and kept separate from the rest of the order.</p>\n<p><strong>Drop-off caterer pros:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Lower staffing footprint, useful for weekday office lunches</li>\n<li>Gluten-free trays typically arrive pre-labelled</li>\n<li>Faster to book than a fully staffed event</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Drop-off caterer cons:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>No chef on site to answer a last-minute cross-contact question</li>\n<li>Menu variety is narrower than a bespoke chef menu</li>\n<li>Reheating and holding times affect texture more than live cooking does</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Dubai offices and casual gatherings where food arrives ready and nobody needs table service.</p>\n<p><strong>Verdict: consider</strong> for a lunch order; <strong>skip</strong> for a sit-down celebration.</p>\n<h2>4. Hotel and restaurant catering arms: best for turnkey venue packages</h2>\n<p>Hotels and restaurants with a catering arm bring an already-tested gluten-free menu and, often, the venue itself. That&#39;s useful when one contract needs to cover food, space and service together, but the gluten-free choices are limited to whatever&#39;s already on that kitchen&#39;s standing menu.</p>\n<p><strong>Hotel catering pros:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Menu already tested at volume, so consistency is more predictable</li>\n<li>Venue and catering can come from a single contract</li>\n<li>Front-of-house staff usually trained on the venue&#39;s own allergen list</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Hotel catering cons:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Gluten-free choices limited to what&#39;s already on the house menu</li>\n<li>Less flexibility to swap in a specific dish you had in mind</li>\n<li>The personal menu conversation a private chef offers isn&#39;t part of the format</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Best for:</strong> events already booked into a hotel or restaurant venue, where catering comes bundled with the space.</p>\n<p><strong>Verdict: book</strong> if the venue is already decided; <strong>skip</strong> if you&#39;re choosing the caterer first.</p>\n<h2>How we ranked</h2>\n<p>Each option sits against the six criteria above — ingredient transparency, separate prep, genuine menu flexibility, halal alignment, staffing awareness and scale match. None of the four wins across every scenario; the ranking reflects which gluten-free situation each format actually solves in Dubai in 2026, not a single universal winner.</p>\n<div class=\"pseo-quote\" style=\"display:flow-root;clear:both;margin:32px 0;padding:24px 28px;border-left:3px solid;border-left-color:rgba(128,128,128,0.6);border-left-color:color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 30%, transparent);border-radius:12px;background-color:rgba(128,128,128,0.06);background-color:color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 4%, transparent);max-width:100%;\"><p style=\"margin:0;font-size:19px;font-weight:500;font-style:normal;line-height:1.5;color:inherit;\">“The safest gluten-free plan is the one where you set the menu with the chef, not the one where you hope the caterer got it right.”</p></div><h2>Which gluten-free caterer should you choose in 2026?</h2>\n<p>For most households and small offices weighing up gluten-free catering in Dubai, <strong>myCHEF is the default starting point</strong>: the chef discusses your ingredient list before the booking, and the same relationship covers a one-off dinner or a recurring weekly menu. Move to a full-service event caterer once the guest list passes what one kitchen can manage. Choose a drop-off specialist for a weekday lunch, and let the venue decide if you&#39;ve already booked a hotel or restaurant space for the event.</p>\n<div class=\