+  "body_html": "<p>A gluten-free event menu requires clear ingredient and preparation questions. Explain each guest’s requirements and ask the provider about feasible controls, labels and cross-contact limitations.</p>\n<p>For the service options, explore <a href=\"/catering-dubai\">catering services in Dubai</a>. Use this guide to prepare the details for your enquiry.</p>\n<h2>Explain the guest requirements clearly</h2>\n<p>Tell the provider which guests require gluten-free food and whether they have coeliac disease, a wheat allergy or another requirement. These should not be treated as interchangeable. Follow the guest’s or their clinician’s instructions rather than assuming that a menu label alone answers the brief.</p>\n<h2>Ask about every component</h2>\n<p>Discuss sauces, dressings, stocks, coatings, garnishes and bought-in ingredients as well as the main dishes. Ask how ingredient information is checked and how substitutions will be communicated before service. Keep the approved menu and dietary notes together.</p>\n<h2>Discuss preparation and cross-contact limits</h2>\n<p>Ask about preparation surfaces, utensils, storage and cooking equipment. The provider should explain what separation is feasible and what limitations remain. A private kitchen, a production kitchen and a buffet have different practical constraints; none should be described as risk-free without evidence.</p>\n<h2>Plan labels and serving responsibilities</h2>\n<p>Agree how the required meals will be identified and handed to the correct guests. Ask who answers ingredient questions during service and how serving utensils will be managed. Avoid expecting guests to make decisions from the appearance of a dish.</p>\n<h2>Compare scope rather than rankings</h2>\n<p>Assess each proposal against the same written requirements. A claim to be the best gluten-free caterer is less useful than a clear explanation of ingredients, preparation and service. Do not rely on unsupported ratings or assume that a dietary request can always be accommodated.</p>\n<h2>Confirm feasibility before booking</h2>\n<p>Explore <a href=\"/allergy-safe-catering-dubai\">allergy-aware catering and dietary planning</a> and ask the team to assess the requirements. The written response should identify the agreed menu and any limitations before the booking is confirmed.</p>",
+  "body_markdown": "A gluten-free event menu requires clear ingredient and preparation questions. Explain each guest’s requirements and ask the provider about feasible controls, labels and cross-contact limitations.\n\nFor the service options, explore [catering services in Dubai](/catering-dubai). Use this guide to prepare the details for your enquiry.\n\n## Explain the guest requirements clearly\nTell the provider which guests require gluten-free food and whether they have coeliac disease, a wheat allergy or another requirement. These should not be treated as interchangeable. Follow the guest’s or their clinician’s instructions rather than assuming that a menu label alone answers the brief.\n\n## Ask about every component\nDiscuss sauces, dressings, stocks, coatings, garnishes and bought-in ingredients as well as the main dishes. Ask how ingredient information is checked and how substitutions will be communicated before service. Keep the approved menu and dietary notes together.\n\n## Discuss preparation and cross-contact limits\nAsk about preparation surfaces, utensils, storage and cooking equipment. The provider should explain what separation is feasible and what limitations remain. A private kitchen, a production kitchen and a buffet have different practical constraints; none should be described as risk-free without evidence.\n\n## Plan labels and serving responsibilities\nAgree how the required meals will be identified and handed to the correct guests. Ask who answers ingredient questions during service and how serving utensils will be managed. Avoid expecting guests to make decisions from the appearance of a dish.\n\n## Compare scope rather than rankings\nAssess each proposal against the same written requirements. A claim to be the best gluten-free caterer is less useful than a clear explanation of ingredients, preparation and service. Do not rely on unsupported ratings or assume that a dietary request can always be accommodated.\n\n## Confirm feasibility before booking\nExplore [allergy-aware catering and dietary planning](/allergy-safe-catering-dubai) and ask the team to assess the requirements. The written response should identify the agreed menu and any limitations before the booking is confirmed.",
